31,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some scary numbers! Transport and insurance are eating up a huge chunk of our installation budget, and the cost for custom mounts is skyrocketing. We really need to be careful!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings are equally concerning. The conservation lab is severely understaffed, with a massive backlog of pieces waiting for stabilization. We are operating with far fewer professional hands than we assume.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shion,,It seems we are focusing on the costs of the process. I found that visitors are bored by static displays; they return for interactive elements or a human presence in the gallery.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The physical constraints are a liability. The suspended bay has a strict weight limit, and our evening hire bookings mean the gallery must remain functional for events, which puts fragile or open displays at risk.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have quite a few hurdles to clear, doesn't it? I've noticed that paperwork delays from distant lenders have caused openings to slip, and our powered displays have been rather temperamental lately.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, if the lab is that backed up, we can't afford an exhibition with lots of fragile pieces that need stabilization, right? That would just add to the stress!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"Exactly, Mio. Any project requiring extensive conservation work before opening would be a significant risk. We must prioritize exhibitions that don't rely on a lab that is already overwhelmed.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, if the suspended bay is a liability and the evening hires are frequent, we should avoid anything that requires a static, fragile environment. It would be a waste of the space's potential.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, it is not just about potential, but about risk. We cannot promise a space to a curator if the floor cannot support the weight or if event caterers might damage the exhibits.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, @Victoria, you both make such important points. It would be a shame to put our wonderful staff under too much pressure. We should look for something that lets them breathe a little.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, I totally agree! And since custom mounts and shipping are so expensive now, maybe we should look for a show that uses objects already in our collection or things that come with their own stands?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, that is a rational approach. Furthermore, we must consider the volunteers. Most are local historians, not trained handlers, so we cannot rely on them for technical installation or specialized care.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, if the volunteers are limited, then a show that requires constant, specialized supervision is a failure waiting to happen. We need something that draws a crowd without draining our few experts.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, I agree. We must avoid any proposal that requires heavy structural shoring or permanent installations that block the gallery's use for evening hires. The space must remain a functional building.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Asuka, you are so right to think of the building's needs. I also worry that if we rely on complex electronics or distant lenders, we might find ourselves apologizing to guests at the door again. Let's be gentle with our plans.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm feeling a bit overwhelmed by all these risks! It sounds like we need a project that is light on the budget, easy on the staff, and doesn't break the floor. Let's hope the candidates fit that!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"It is a daunting list of constraints, but it provides a clear filter. We need a proposal that is structurally light, conservation-neutral, and operationally simple. Let us see which candidate actually respects our current capacity.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shion,,"It is simple, really. We just need to stop pretending that a prestigious list of objects equals a successful show. If the gallery is dead, the prestige is meaningless. Let us see if any candidate actually understands the audience.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Asuka,,We have established a clear set of operational boundaries. Any candidate that ignores the weight limits of the suspended bay or the logistical reality of our evening hires is an unacceptable risk. Logic must dictate our choice.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"Now, now, let's not be too overwhelmed, dear Mio. We have all worked together to find the pitfalls, and that is the first step to a happy outcome. I am sure we will find a lovely exhibition that makes everyone smile.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
